  "designConstraints": [
    "Validate every original directory range and ordering, including unconsumed tables; preserve eager first-error order.",
    "Retain every current static consumer, including optional kern/vhea/vmtx and GDEF/GPOS/GSUB; no glyph or required-script subsetting.",
    "Reserve owned capacity before allocation and preserve independent backing, terminal refusal and cleanup; no cache of caller bytes.",
    "Do not full-copy first and then compact: overlapping old/new ownership would add a replacement peak and repeat the expensive copy.",
    "Do not skip directory checks or treat an unretained range as truncated after compaction; rebasing must be private and bounds-proven.",
    "Retained table spans and relative offsets must survive independently until final font disposal; prepared layouts must still survive font disposal.",
    "Preserve load input/working/container limits, structured failures, cancelable validation loops and exact glyph/outline/layout observations.",
    "No reference/fixture change: measure the original complete owned load against the same FreeType 2.13.2 copy/open/retain/dispose boundary.",
    "A promising private complete-operation screen requires independent confirmation and final affected font/text reconciliation before broad/package qualification."
  ],
  "decision": "Prepare a bounded private directory-driven compaction design next. This audit establishes byte/lifetime headroom only, not an accepted implementation or CPU saving. Keep canonical production and all current measurements unchanged.",
